member.summary:
How a CLI must launch the AutoCAD MCP server (the bridge, AcadCopilotMcp.exe) for this turn.
Runners turn this into per-invocation MCP configuration and never touch the user's global config:
Claude Code: --mcp-config <file or JSON> --strict-mcp-config;
Codex: -c mcp_servers.<ServerName>.command=... -c mcp_servers.<ServerName>.args=[...] (TOML values);
Gemini: settings.json "mcpServers" in a private workspace folder.

System instructions given to every CLI turn (Claude Code: --append-system-prompt-file; Codex: developer_instructions;
Gemini CLI: GEMINI.md in its private workspace). They decide how the AI drafts: AutoCAD's own commands typed through
run_commands, checked with capture_view, in stages the user can follow.

Classifies one input of a step on its own: AutoLISP ("(" or "!"), a transparent command ("'NAME", classified
like a command) or a protected system variable name. Anything else is Allowed (its effect depends on the prompt;
the drafting engine checks spaces against the live prompt).

            THE CONTRACT BETWEEN THE CHAT VIEW MODEL AND EVERYTHING ELSE. The add-in's PaneController creates one
             and passes it to the CopilotPane view; the view model:


calls  with its  implementation (questions, plan, approvals);

lists  for the provider picker and their  for the model picker;

calls  to show "Signed in / Sign in" per provider and  for the button;

calls  for each user message and renders the  stream
            (TextDelta/TextDone = assistant text, ToolCallStarted/Finished = "CAD activity" rows, TurnFailed = error banner);
            Stop = cancel the token passed to ;

calls  for the New chat button.

            Events may be raised on any thread; marshal to the WPF dispatcher.

Applies the AI's labels: each label names the drawing that contains its point (or the nearest one within
). Unrecognised titles make the drawing kind Other with that title. Returns the new list
and the labels that matched no drawing.
